  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 1235 PM CST Thu Nov 19 2026\n\nAttention in the long term is on late Saturday into Sunday\nmorning when a shortwave and strong cold front will bring rain\nchances and a minimal chance of non-severe thunderstorms. Rain\nchances are currently 50-100% from the NBM, lowest over south-\ncentral MO and highest over SE KS and western MO. NBM\nprobabilities for rainfall amounts are 40-100% for >= 0.10\" and\n20-80% for >= 0.25%, both with a similar distribution pattern to\nthe PoP. Precip should be mostly out of the CWA by Sunday\nafternoon. \n\nFollowing the cold front, look much cooler conditions with highs\ngenerally in the 50s Sunday and Monday and the 40s Tuesday and\nWednesday. Lows will be in the 20s and 30s starting Sunday\nnight, then potentially in the teens in some spots starting\nTuesday night. \n\nTo address some hype of a potential wintry system after\nThanksgiving, confidence in any outcomes is extremely low.\nEnsembles show a very wide range of solutions, even for the \noverall large scale pattern. In other words, there is no\nreason to message a potential system at this point.",
